hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7426","7471 Ahmad bin Saeed told us, Al-Ahwas told us, he said: Ammar bin Ruzaiq told us, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, he said: On the authority of Al-Harith, and Abi Maysarah, on the authority of Ali, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say when he lay down: “O God, I seek refuge in Your generous face and in Your words.” Complete of the evil that you are taking by the corner of it, O God, you remove the debt and the sin, O God, may your soldier not be defeated, nor break your promise, nor The grandfather will benefit from you, glory be to You and praise be to You.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7427","7472 Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah told me, he said: My father told me, he said: Ibrahim told me, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of my father Al-Zinad, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that he heard him say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The right hand of God is full, no He enriches it with spending in the light of the night and the day. He said: Have you seen what has been spent since the creation of the heavens and the earth? He has not neglected what is in His right hand. He said: And his throne is on the water, and in his other hand is the scales, which he lowers and raises.”"
"7428","7473 Qutaibah bin Sa’id informed us, saying: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Ibn Yasar, that he heard Abu Hurairah, saying The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “No one gives in charity any good thing, and God does not accept anything but good things, except that the Most Merciful takes it with His right hand.” And if it is a date, then let it grow in the palm of the Most Gracious, until it is greater than a mountain, just as one of you raises his foal or his offspring.”"
"7429","7474 Ali bin Shuaib told us, he said: Ma’n told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever gives charity from good earnings, and God accepts only good things, it is as if He creates it in the palm of the Most Gracious, and nurtures it as one of you nurtures his foal or his offspring, until it becomes like a mountain.”"
"7430","7475 Ali bin Hajar informed us, he said: I am Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “Habr came From the Jews to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: When the Day of Resurrection comes, God will place the heavens on a finger, and the earths on a finger. And the mountains and trees are on a finger, and the water and the earth are on a finger, and all creatures are on a finger, then he shakes them and says: I am the king. I am the king. I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughing, and God, Blessed and Most High, revealed: “And they have not esteemed God according to His esteem.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7431","7476 Al-Hasan bin Ahmad told us, he said: Abu Al-Rabi’ narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to us, Al-Mu’alla bin Ziyad, and Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Aisha, said: “I used to hear the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, frequently praying with it: O Converter of hearts, make my heart firm on Your religion. I said: O Messenger of God, I see you and I hear you often supplicate: O the converter of hearts, make my heart steadfast in your religion. He said: “There is no human being who does not have his heart between two of God’s fingers. If He wills, He can make it straight, and if He wills, He can make it move.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7432","7477 Muhammad bin Hatim told us, he said: Hibban told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, he said: I heard a secret Bin Ubayd Allah, saying: I heard Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, saying: I heard Al-Nawwas bin Samaan Al-Kalabi, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, he says: “There is no heart except between two of the fingers of the Most Gracious. If He wills, He can make it straight, and if He wills, He can make it move.” And the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was May God bless him and grant him peace. He says: Oh God, the converter of hearts, make our hearts firm upon Your religion, and the scales are in the hand of the Most Gracious. He raises peoples and lowers others until the Day of Resurrection.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7433","7478 Muhammad bin Hatim told us, he said: I am Suwayd, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Haywa bin Shurayh, he said: Abu Hani Al-Khawlani informed me He heard Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubli saying: I heard Abdullah bin Amr saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He says: “The hearts of the children of Adam are between two of the fingers of the Most Gracious, like one heart, which it can configure as it pleases.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says And peace be upon him: O God, the Converter of hearts, direct our hearts to obey You. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7434","7479 Imran bin Bakkar told us, he said: Ali bin Ayyash told us, he said: Shuaib told me, he said: Abu Al-Zannad told me, from what Abdul told him The Most Gracious, the most lame, from what he mentioned, is that he heard Abu Hurairah narrating it, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: And he said: “You have argued Paradise and Hell. Hell said: I am influenced by the arrogant and arrogant. Paradise said: What is the matter with me? Only the weak and the fallen will enter me. And I failed them, so God, Blessed and Most High, said to Paradise: You are only a mercy, meaning, I will have mercy on you whomever I please of My servants, and He said to Hell: It is only You are a torment, I punish with you whomever I wish, and each one of you has its own full, but as for fire: it will not be filled until the Most Gracious, the Almighty, puts in it He presented it, and He says: “Quit” and you say: “Quot,” So there it will be filled and some of it will be aligned with the other. As for Paradise: God will not be unjust to whoever. He created him as one.”"
"7435","7480 Muhammad bin Ubaid bin Muhammad informed us, saying: Ali bin Mushar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Suwayd, On the authority of Abdullah, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “God is more happy with the repentance of His servant than a man whose camel goes astray.” A deadly Bedouin woman who was in charge of his food and drink. He asked for her until, when the effort reached, he said: I will return to the place of my departure and die there. Then he returned. So he stood up, and suddenly his mount was at his head, carrying his food and drink.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7436","7481 Ahmad bin Harb informed us, saying: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Suwayd, and Al-Aswad, saying: We told him Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “To God, I am happier with the repentance of one of you than a man who emerged from a devastating, destructive land.” And his camel was with him, carrying his food and provisions and what he could use, so he led it astray, so he went out in search of it until death overtook him, saying: Return to the place Wherein I had led her astray, and I would die. So he returned to his place, and his eyes overcame him. He woke up and saw his mount at his head, with his food on it. And his drink, and his provisions, and what improves him.”"
"7437","7482 Muhammad bin Ubaid bin Muhammad informed us, saying: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara bin Umayr, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Suwayd, On the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, similar to his saying: “And his drink, and he did not mention what came after it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7438","7483 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zinad, and Muhammad bin Salamah informed us, saying: Ibn Al-Qasim told us, on the authority of Malik, he said: Abu Al-Zinad told me, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God, Blessed be He, said And God Almighty says: If My servant loves meeting Me, I love meeting him, and if My servant hates meeting Me, I hate meeting him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7439","7484 Ali bin Hajar informed us, he said: I am Ismail, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he is Ibn Saree’, and he was a poet, he said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “O Messenger of God, shall I not call upon you to praise my Lord with it?” He said: “Indeed, your Lord loves Al-Muhammad, and he did not add anything to that.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7440","7485 Ali bin Hajar informed us, he said: I am Ismail, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakra, he said: Ashjaj Bani Asr said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “Indeed, there are two qualities in you that God loves.” I said: What are they? He said: Forbearance and modesty. He said: Ancient times. Was it recent? He said: No, but in the past. I said: Praise be to God who created me with two creatures that God loves."
"7441","7486 Qutaibah bin Sa’id informed us, saying: Ya’qub told us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And peace be upon him, he said: “If God loves a servant, he calls Gabriel and says: I loved so-and-so, so love him, and Gabriel loves him, then he calls Gabriel, the inhabitants of heaven: “Indeed, God loves so-and-so, so they love him, then He assigns for him acceptance on earth, and hatred like that.”"
"7442","7487 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abdah bin Sulaiman, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Omar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, On the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I lost the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one night, and I came to him while he was He is prostrating with his feet upright, and he is saying: “O God, I seek refuge in You in Your pleasure from Your anger, and in Your pardon from Your punishment. I cannot count the praise.” On you, just as you praised yourself.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7443","7488 Amr bin Yahya bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Abu Salih told us, he said: Ibn Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Zaid Ibn Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ Ibn Yasar, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God says to the people of Paradise: O people of Paradise, and they will say: At your service, our Lord, and we are pleased with you. He will say: Are you satisfied? They will say: Why should we not be satisfied, even though we have been satisfied? You have given us what you have not given to any of your creation. He says: I give you better than that. They said: O Lord, and what thing is better than that? I will bestow upon you My pleasure, and I will never be displeased with you after that.”"
"7444","7489 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Al-Mughirah bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zannad, and Ahmad bin Hafs informed us, saying: My father told me, he said: Abraham told me, on the authority of Moses, he said: Abu Al-Zinad told me, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “When God decreed creation, He wrote in His Book, while He was with Him above the Throne: Indeed, My mercy has prevailed over My wrath.” The wording is by Qutaybah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7445","7490 Mahmoud bin Ghaylan informed us, saying: Waki’ told us, and Abu Dawud Al-Hafari, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When God had finished creating, He wrote on His throne: Indeed, my mercy precedes my wrath,” he said. Abu Dawud: My mercy overcomes my wrath, and he is above the throne"
"7446","7491 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak informed us, saying: Suleiman bin Harb told us, and Hisham bin Abdul-Malik told us, they said: Hammad told us, Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Al-Walid told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Amr, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Harith. On the authority of Ali, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say at the end of his Witr prayer: I seek refuge, and Muhammad said: O God, I seek refuge in Your satisfaction from Your anger, and I seek refuge in you to recover from your punishment, and I seek refuge in you from you, I do not praise you enough, you are as you praised yourself.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7447","7492 Muhammad ibn Salamah informed us, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “ The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led the people in prayer and delivered a sermon, then he left, then He said: O nation of Muhammad, there is no one more jealous than God if His servant commits adultery, or his female slave commits adultery,” in brief. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7448","7493 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Yahya bin Adam, he said: Issa bin Tahman told us, he said: I heard Anas bin Malik, saying: “ Zainab used to be proud of the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: God granted me sex from heaven. Yahya said: What do you mean by God’s saying: \"We married her to you\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7449","7494 Qutaibah ibn Sa`id informed us, on the authority of Malik and al-Harith ibn Miskin, reading it, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik narrated to me, on the authority of Hilal Ibn Usama, on the authority of Ata’ Ibn Yasar, on the authority of Omar Ibn Al-Hakam, he said: “I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, A maid of mine was taking care of sheep for me, so I came to her and found a sheep from the sheep missing. I asked her about it, and she said: The wolf ate it, so I was sorry. And I was one of the children of Adam, so I slapped her face while I had a slave. Should I free her? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: Where is God? She said: In heaven. He said: Who am I? She said: You are the Messenger of God. He said: Free her."
"7450","7495 Shuaib bin Shuaib bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Yahya, he said: Malik told us, he said: Abu Al-Zinad told me, on the authority of Al-Araj, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When God decreed creation, He wrote in His Book, while He was with Him above the Throne: Indeed, My mercy precedes My wrath.”"
"7451","7496 Muhammad bin Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Muhammad, he said: Abraham told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, and Abdul Rahman Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not give me a choice over Moses, for people will be shocked on the Day of Resurrection. So I will be the first to wake up, then suddenly Moses is standing next to the throne. I do not know whether he was struck and woke up before me, or whether he was among those whom God Almighty made an exception. Glory be to Him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7452","7497 Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “No Muslim gives in charity anything that is good, and God does not accept anything but a good thing, and no one ascends to heaven except a good thing.” It is as if he places it in the palm of the Most Gracious, and nurtures it as a man nurtures his foal or his offspring, until the date returns like a great mountain.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7453","7498 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, and Al-Harith bin Miskin, reading it, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of my father Al-Zinad, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Angels follow one another among you at night, And angels by day, and they gather for the dawn prayer, then those who spent the night among you come back, and He asks them, and He knows best about them: How? Did you leave My servants, and they say: We left them while they were praying, and We came to them while they were praying.” The wording is by Qutaybah."
"7454","7499 Abdah bin Abdullah told us, he said: I am Husayn, he said: Zaida told us, he said: Bayan bin Bishr told us, on the authority of Qais, he said: Jarir told us. He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to us on the night of the full moon, and he looked at the moon and said: You see your Lord as you see it.” This, you will not be troubled about seeing it.”"
"7455","7500 Muhammad bin Muammar told us, he said: Yahya bin Kathir told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, and Abdullah bin Uthman told us, they said: Ismail bin Kathir told us. Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of Jarir bin Abdullah, who said: “We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one night. So our eyes became clear, so he made us look at the moon on the night of the full moon, and he said: But you will look at your Lord as you look at the moon. Do not be sure of seeing it. If you are able not to miss two prayers, then do it: a prayer before sunrise, and a prayer before it sets. And he recited: “And glorify the praise of your Lord.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7456","7501 Amr bin Yazid told us, he said: Saif bin Ubaid Allah told us, he said: He was trustworthy, on the authority of Salamah bin Ayyar, on the authority of Saeed bin Abd Al-Aziz, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: We said: O Messenger of God, will we see our Lord? He said: Do you see the sun on a day with no clouds, and do you see the moon on a night with no clouds? We said: Yes. He said: Indeed, you will see your Lord."
"7457","7502 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Baqiyya bin Al-Walid, he said: Buhair bin Saad told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Ma’dan, on the authority of Amr Ibn Al-Aswad, that Junada Ibn Abi Umayyah told them, on the authority of Ubadah Ibn Al-Samit, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “I I told you about the Antichrist until I feared that you would not understand him. He is short, coarse, wrinkled, one-eyed, and his left eye is not visible. And do not be stoned. If there is confusion for you, know that your Lord, Blessed and Most High, is not one-eyed, and that you will not see your Lord until you die.”"
"7458","7503 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abu Abd al-Samad told us, he said: Abu Imran al-Juni told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Qais Al-Ash’ari, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Two gardens of silver, their utensils and what is in them, and two gardens of “The gold of their vessels and what is in them, and there is nothing between the people and them seeing their Lord except the veil of pride over His face in the Garden of Eden.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7459","7504 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila, On the authority of Suhayb, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in this verse: “For those who do good, goodness and more. He said: When the people of Paradise enter: Paradise, and the people of Hell: Hell. They will proclaim: O people of Paradise, indeed there is a promise for you with God. They said: What is it? Has not God made our faces white? And He makes our scales heavy, and admits us to Paradise, and saves us from the Fire, then He removes the veil and appears to them. By God, God has not given them anything. more beloved to them than looking at him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7460","7505 Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, reading it, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Abu Al-Zannad, on the authority of Al-Araj On the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God laughs at two men, one of whom kills the other. Paradise, this man fights in the cause of God and is killed, then God turns to the killer, so he fights and is martyred.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7461","7506 Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ibn al-Qasim told us, on the authority of Malik, he said: Ibn Shihab told us, on the authority of Abu Abdullah al-Aghar, and my father Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Every night God Almighty descends to the lowest heaven until He remains The last third of the night, and He says: Whoever calls upon Me, that I may respond to him, whoever asks of Me, I will give to him, whoever asks Me for forgiveness, that I may forgive him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7462","7507 Imran bin Bakkar told us, he said: Muhammad bin Al-Mubarak Al-Souri told us, he said: Yahya bin Hassan told us, on the authority of Hushaym, on the authority of Ismail. Ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qays, said: “I saw Muawiyah who had recovered from an illness that had taken him while he was giving the sermon, and he had uncovered his arms and they were It is as if they were the branches of palm trees, and he says: Is this world anything but what we have tasted and experienced? By God, I wish I had no choice among you beyond three, even more than three. God has corrected it, so a man stood up to him and said: To the mercy of God, O Commander of the Faithful. He said: Rather, to what God willed for me, and God knows that I did not Deviate from the truth, and if God disliked anything, He would change it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7463","7508 Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn Al-Samit, on the authority of Ubadah bin Al-Samit, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pledged allegiance to us on hearing and obedience: in times of ease and hardship. And the motivator, and the compulsive, and not to dispute the matter with its people, and to uphold what is right wherever we are, not fearing, for God’s sake, the blame of the blamer.”"
"7464","7509 Issa bin Hammad informed us, saying: Al-Layth bin Saad informed us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Ubadah bin Al-Walid bin Ubadah. Ibn Al-Samit, on the authority of his father, that Ubadah Ibn Al-Samit said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pledged allegiance to us on listening and obedience: in hardship. “And ease, and what is motivating, and what is compulsory, and not to dispute the matter with its people, and to uphold what is right wherever we are, not fearing, for God’s sake, the blame of the blamer.”"
"7465","7510 Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin informed us of a reading from him while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim. He said: Malik told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: Ubadah bin Al-Walid bin Ubadah told me, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Ubadah bin Al-Samit, he said: “ We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to listen and obey: in ease, in hardship, in good times, in times of need, and not to dispute the matter. His family, and to speak or do what is right wherever we are, not fearing the blame of the blamer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7466","7511 Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Abu Usama told us, he said: Al-Walid bin Kathir told me, he said: Ubadah bin Al-Waleed, that his father Al-Waleed told him, on the authority of his grandfather, Ubadah bin Al-Samit, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pledged allegiance to us on the basis of hearing And obedience in: our hardship, our ease, our hardships, and our hardships, and not to dispute the matter with its people, and to say with justice wherever we are, no “We fear, for God’s sake, the blame of the blamer.”"
"7467","7512 Muhammad bin Yahya bin Ayyub informed us, saying: Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, and Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pledged allegiance to us upon hearing And obedience in: hardship, ease, motivating factor, compulsion, and the influence upon us, and so long as we do not dispute the matter with its people, and so long as we say: “Indeed, where we were.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7468","7513 Muhammad ibn al-Walid informed us, saying: Muhammad informed us, saying: Shu`bah informed us, on the authority of Sayyar, and Yahya ibn Sa`id al-Qadi, that they They heard Ubadah ibn al-Walid speaking, on the authority of his father. As for Sayyar, he spoke on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. As for Yahya, He said: On the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pledged allegiance to us on hearing and obedience in: our hardship and our ease. Our motivator, our compulsion, and the influence upon us, and not to dispute the matter with its people, and to uphold what is right wherever it is, not fearing God’s blame. Layim,” Shu’bah said: Sayyar did not mention this letter: wherever it was, so Yahya mentioned it. Shu’bah said: If I added anything to it, then it is On the authority of Sayyar, or on the authority of Yahya (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7469","7514 Qutaibah bin Sa’id informed us, saying: Ya’qub told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “You must obey in: what motivates you, what compels you, what is difficult for you, what makes you happy, and what is preferable to you.”"
"7470","7515 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid informed us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqah, on the authority of Jarir, he said: “I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him and grant him advice to every Muslim.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7471","7516 Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ibn Ulayya told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Amr bin Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah bin Amr. Ibn Jarir, Jarir said: “I pledged allegiance to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to listen and obey, and to advise every Muslim.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7472","7517 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, he heard Jabir say: “We did not pledge allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him upon death. We only pledged our pledge to him that we would not flee.”"
"7473","7518 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hatim told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ubaid, he said: I said to Salamah bin Al-Akwa’: “For anything.” Did you pledge allegiance to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Hudaybiyyah? He said: On death? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7474","7519 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Qais told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Abdullah, he said: “I pledged allegiance The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was required to establish prayer, pay zakat, and advise every Muslim.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7475","7520 Ahmad ibn Amr informed us, saying: Ibn Wahb informed us, saying: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Amr Ibn Abd al-Rahman Ibn Umayyah, my nephew, Ali Ibn Umayyah, told him that his father told him that Ya`la Ibn Umayyah said: “I came as a messenger May God’s prayers and peace be upon Abu Umayyah on the day of the conquest, so I said: O Messenger of God, pledge allegiance to my father on the emigration, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Rather, I pledge allegiance to him for jihad, and migration has ended.”"
"7476","7521 Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Mushar told us, he said: Saeed bin Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Rabi’ah bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Abu Muslim Al-Khawlani, said: The beloved and trustworthy Awf bin Malik Al-Ashja’i told me, he said: “We were with the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: Will you not pledge allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him? He repeated it three times, so we presented our hands and he pledged allegiance to us, so we said. He said: O Messenger of God, we have pledged our pledge of allegiance to you, so for what? He said: “On the condition that you worship God, and do not associate anything with Him, and the five daily prayers.” He mentioned a light word, no. “Ask people something.”"
"7477","7522 Ubayd Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, he said: My uncle told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Abu Idris Al-Khawlani told me that Ubadah bin Al-Samit said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, ‘And around him was a band of His companions: You pledge your allegiance to me on the condition that you do not associate anything with God, do not commit adultery, do not steal, do not kill your children, and do not commit slander. You invent it between your hands and your feet, and do not disobey me in what is right. So whoever fulfills it, his reward will be with God, and whoever among you does something wrong will be punished for it. This world, it is an atonement for him, and whoever does any of that, then God will cover him, so his matter is up to God. If He wills, He will pardon him, and if He wills. He punished him.” Ahmad bin Saeed disagreed with him. He narrated it on the authority of Ya’qub, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Fudayl, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, About worship, sent"
"7478","Ahmad bin Saeed told me, he said: Ya’qub told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Fudayl, that Ibn Shihab He told him, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Will you not pledge allegiance to me on what the women pledged allegiance on, that you do not associate God anything, and do not steal, and do not commit adultery, and do not kill your children, and do not bring any slander that you invent between your hands and your feet, and do not Do you disobey me in a good deed? We said: Yes, O Messenger of God, so we pledged allegiance to him on that, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who did the right thing after that? If a punishment befalls him for it, then it is an expiation. And whoever does not suffer a punishment for it, then his matter is up to God. If He wills, He will forgive him, and if He wills, He will punish. \"with it\""
"7479","7524 Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi informed us, saying: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, “A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “O Messenger of God, I have come to pledge allegiance to you on immigration, and I have left my parents.” They were crying. He said: Go back to them and make them laugh as you made them cry. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7480","7525 Al-Hussein bin Harith told us, he said: Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yazid Al-Laythi added, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, “A Bedouin asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about immigration, and he said: Woe to you, if there is a The migration is difficult. Do you have any camels? He said: Yes. He said: Will you pay their zakat? He said: Yes. He said: Work from beyond the seas, for God is the One. God Almighty will not leave anything of your work behind.”"
"7481","7526 Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam told us, saying: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, On the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Kathir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: A man said: “O Messenger of God, that is, migration Is it better? He said: To abandon what God Almighty detests, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The migration is two migrations: the migration of the present. And the migration of the deserter. As for the deserter: he obeys when ordered and responds when called. As for the present: he is the greater of the two in calamity. And the best of them in reward.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7482","7527 Al-Hussein bin Mansour bin Jaafar told us, he said: Mubasher bin Abdullah told us, he said: Sufyan bin Hussein told us, on the authority of Ya’la bin Muslim, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, said: Ibn Abbas said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in Mecca, and Abu Bakr, Omar was among the emigrants, because they abandoned the polytheists, and he was among the Ansar, the emigrants, because Medina was a house of polytheism, so they came to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the night of Aqaba.”"
"7483","7528 Harun bin Muhammad bin Bakkar bin Bilal informed me, on the authority of Muhammad, who is the son of Isa bin Al-Qasim bin Sami, he said: Zaid told us, on the authority of Kathir ibn Murrah said that Abu Fatima told him that he said: “O Messenger of God, tell me about a deed that I can do correctly and know.” He said to him: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: You must emigrate, for there is nothing like it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7484","7529 Abd Al-Malik bin Shuaib bin Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: Aqeel told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, On the authority of Amr bin Abdul Rahman bin Umayyah, that his father told him that Ya’la bin Umayyah said: “I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted Abu Umayyah on the day of the conquest, and I said: O Messenger of God, pledge allegiance to my father on the migration. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Yes. “I pledge allegiance to him for jihad, while migration has ended?”"
"7485","7530 Muhammad bin Dawud told me, he said: Mu’alla bin Asad told us, he said: Wahib bin Khaled told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Tawus, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Safwan bin Umayyah, he said: I said: “O Messenger of God, they say: No one will enter Paradise except those who emigrate.” He said: No. Migration after the conquest of Mecca, but jihad with intention, and when you are mobilized, then mobilize.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7486","7531 Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Mansour told me, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the day of the Conquest: “No emigration, but jihad and intention, and if “If you are called out, then go out.”"
"7487","7532 Amr bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Hani, on the authority of Nu’aym bin Dajaja, He said: I heard Omar bin Al-Khattab saying: “There is no migration after the death of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"7488","7533 Issa bin Musawar told us, he said: Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Ala, on the authority of Busr bin Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Waqqadan Al-Saadi, said: “I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a delegation, all of us asking for something. I was the last of them to enter the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said: O Messenger of God, I left those behind me while they claim that Migration has stopped. He said: Migration will not stop as long as the infidels are killed.”"
"7489","7534 Mahmoud bin Khalid told us, he said: Marwan bin Muhammad told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Ala bin Zubr told us, he said: he told me Busr bin Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Hassan bin Abdullah Al-Dhamri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Saadi, he said: “Our delegation On the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so my companions entered and fulfilled their needs, then I was the last of them to enter, and he said: I need you, so I said: O Messenger God, when will the migration stop? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The migration will not stop as long as the infidels are killed. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7490","7535 Muhammad ibn Qudamah told me, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, and al-Sha’bi, they said: Jarir said: “I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Ali, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I said to him: I pledge my allegiance to you on the basis of listening and obedience in what I like and in what I dislike. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Or you can That, O Jarir, can you bear that? He said: Say what you can, so he pledged allegiance to me, and sincere advice is given to every Muslim. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7491","7536 Bishr bin Khalid told us, he said: Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Sulayman, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Jarir, he said: “I pledged allegiance The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to establish prayer, pay zakat, and be sincere to every Muslim, and to separate from the polytheist.” Muhammad ibn Yahya bin Muhammad, he said: Al-Hasan bin Al-Rabi’ narrated to us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abu Nukhayla, On the authority of Jarir, he said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he mentioned something similar to it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7492","7537 Muhammad bin Qudamah told me, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abu Nakhayla al-Bajli, he said: He said: Jarir: “I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was pledging allegiance, and I said: O Messenger of God, extend your hand so that I may pledge allegiance to you, and stipulate that you I know the condition. He said: I pledge allegiance to you on the condition that you worship God, perform prayer, pay zakat, advise the Muslim, and separate from the polytheist.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7493","7538 Ya’qub bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: Ghandar informed us, he said: Muammar informed us, he said: Ibn Shihab informed us, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani said: I heard Ubadah bin Al-Samit saying: “I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a group of people. He said: I pledge allegiance to you on: That you do not associate anything with God, that you do not steal, that you do not commit adultery, that you do not kill your children, and that you do not bring any slander that you invent before yourselves. And your feet, and do not disobey me in what is right, so whoever of you fulfills it, his reward is with God, and whoever does any of these things will be punished, so it is his purification. And whoever God conceals, that is up to God. If He wills, He will punish him, and if He wills, He will forgive him.”"
"7494","7539 Muhammad bin Mansour told me, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Umm Atiya, she said: “When I wanted to I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I said: O Messenger of God, a woman made me happy in pre-Islamic times, so I will go and make her happy. Then I will come to you and pledge allegiance to you. He said: Go. She said: So I went and helped her, then I came and pledged allegiance to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7495","7540 Al-Hasan bin Ahmad told us, he said: Abu Al-Rabi’ told us, he said: Hammad told us, he said: Ayyub told us, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Umm Attiya, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took the pledge of allegiance from us on the condition that we would not mourn.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7496","7541 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin al-Munkadir, on the authority of Umaima bint Raqiqa, she said: “I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with wives to whom we would pledge allegiance, but the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, enjoined upon us that they should not associate By God, he said: As much as you are able and able, we said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is more merciful to us than we are to ourselves. We said: O Messenger of God, Will you not shake hands with us? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I do not shake hands with women. What I say to one woman is the same as I say to a hundred women. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7497","7542 Ziyad bin Ayyub informed us, saying: Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ali bin Ata, on the authority of a man from the Al-Sharid family, called: Amr, on the authority of His father, he said: “There was a leper in the Thaqif delegation, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent to him: Return, for we have pledged allegiance to you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7498","7543 Abdul Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam told us, saying: Omar bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, on the authority of Al-Harmas bin Ziyad, He said: “I extended my hand to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when I was a boy, so that he might pledge allegiance to me, but he did not pledge allegiance to me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7499","7544 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “A slave came and pledged allegiance to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. upon him and grant him peace upon the migration, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not feel that he was a slave, so his master came and wanted him, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “With his own eyes, he bought him for two black slaves, and then he did not pledge allegiance to anyone until he asked him: ‘Is he a slave?’” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7500","7545 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, “An Arab swore allegiance to the Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the Bedouin fell ill in Medina. The Bedouin came to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and said: O Messenger of God, give me my pledge, but he refused. Then he came to him and said: Give me my pledge, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, refused, so he left. The Bedouin, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The city is like a kiln, it expels its impurity, and its perfume is diffused.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7501","7546 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Hatim told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ubaid, on the authority of Salamah bin Al-Akwa’, “that he entered upon Al-Hajjaj, and he said: O Ibn Al-Akwa’, you turned back on your heels and looked like a mess. He said: No, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave me permission to go to the Bedouins. \""
"7502","7547 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdullah, and Ali bin Hajar told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: “We used to pledge allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the basis of listening and obedience. Then he says: You were able.” Ali said: “As much as you are able.”"
"7503","7548 Al-Hasan bin Muhammad told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Musa bin Uqba told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin A dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: “When we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to listen and obey, he would say to us: As much as you are able.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7504","7549 Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: Sayyar told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Jarir bin Abdullah, he said: “I pledged allegiance to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to listen and obey, so he taught me what I could.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7505","7550 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Umaymah bint Ruqaqiqa, she said: “We pledged allegiance The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, among women, and he said to us: “As much as you are able and able.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7506","7551 Hanad bin Al-Sari informed us, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahb, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abd Rabb The Kaaba, he said: I came to Abdullah bin Amr, and he was sitting in the shade of the Kaaba, and the people were gathered around him, so I heard him say: “ While we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, when we camped at a certain place, some of us struck his tent, when the herald of the Prophet called out, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace: Prayer is comprehensive, so we gathered, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and addressed us, saying: There was no prophet before me who was not It is incumbent on him to guide his nation to what he knows is good for them, and warn them of what he knows to be bad for them, and indeed this nation of yours has been made well-off. At the beginning of it, and at the end of it, calamity will befall them and things they deny, temptation will come, and the believer will say: This is my destruction, then It will be revealed, then the temptation will come, and he will say: This is this, then it will be revealed, so whoever loves to be removed from the Fire and enter Paradise, Let his death overtake him while he believes in God and the Last Day, and let him come to the people whom he would like to be brought to, and whoever pledges allegiance to an imam, So He gave him the touch of his hand and the fruit of his heart, so let him obey him as much as he is able.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7507","7552 Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he is Ibn Al-Harith, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Husayn He said: I heard my grandmother saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying in the Farewell Pilgrimage: “And if an Abyssinian slave were appointed over you, He leads you by the Book of God, so listen to him and obey.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7508","7553 Yusuf bin Sa’id told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ziyad bin Sa’d informed me, that Ibn Shihab He told him that Abu Salamah told him that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever obeys me has “I obey God, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed God, and whoever obeys my prince has obeyed me, and whoever disobeys my prince has disobeyed me.”"
"7509","7554 Al-Hasan bin Muhammad told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, Ibn Jurayj said: Ya’la bin Muslim told me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, On the authority of Ibn Abbas: “O you who have believed, obey God and obey the Messenger.” He said: “It was revealed about Abdullah bin Hudhafah bin Qais bin Adiy. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent him in secret.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7510","7555 Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed bin Kathir bin Dinar informed us, saying: Baqiyya told us, on the authority of Buhair, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ubayy Freely, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Invasion is conquest. As for whoever seeks the face of God, And he obeyed the imam, and spent generously, and avoided corruption, for his sleep and his awakening will have a full reward. As for the one who invades out of hypocrisy and reputation, If he disobeys the Imam and spreads corruption on earth, he will not return with sufficient means.”"
"7511","7556 Imran bin Bakkar told us, he said: Ali bin Ayyash told us, he said: Shuaib told us, he said: Abu Al-Zannad told me, from what he told him Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from what he mentioned, is that he heard Abu Hurairah speaking, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: And he said: “But The imam is a guard, behind whom one fights, and one is protected by it. If he commands fear of God and is just, then he will have a reward for that, and if he commands something else, then “On him is a burden.”"
"7512","7557 Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: I asked Suhail bin Abi Salih, I said: Hadith Amr told us, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’a, on the authority of your father, said: I heard it from the one who narrated it to my father. It was narrated by a man from the people of the Levant called: Ata’ bin Yazid, on the authority of Tamim Al-Dari said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The religion is sincere advice, the religion is sincere advice.” They said: To whom, O Messenger of God? He said: To God. And for His Book, and for His Prophet, and for the Imams of the Muslims.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7513","7558 Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of Ata Ibn Yazid Al-Laythi, on the authority of Tamim Al-Dari, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The religion is advice. Religion is advice. They said: To whom, O Messenger of God? He said: To God, to His Book, to His Messenger, to the leaders of the Muslims, and to their common people."
"7514","7559 Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, he said: Shuaib bin Al-Layth told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam. On the authority of Al-Qaqa’ bin Hakim, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Religion is sincere advice, Religion is sincere advice. They said: To whom, O Messenger of God? He said: To God, to His Book, to His Messenger, and to the leaders of the Muslims. \"And their common people\""
"7515","7560 Abd al-Quddus bin Muhammad told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jahdam told us, he said: Ismail bin Ja’far told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, On the authority of Al-Qaqa’ bin Hakim, on the authority of Sumayy, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Maqsim, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Religion is sincere advice.” They said: “For whom, O Messenger of God?” He said: “For God’s sake, for His Book, for His Messenger, and for the leaders of the Muslims.” \"And for their common people\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7516","7561 Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah told us, he said: Muammar bin Yamar told us, he said: Muawiyah, meaning Ibn Salam, told me, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, he said: Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What There is no friend except that he has two companions: a companion who commands him to do good and forbids him from evil, and a companion who does not deceive him, so whoever is protected from its evil He was protected, and he was one of the ones that prevailed over him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7517","7562 Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “God has not sent a prophet, nor has he succeeded anyone.” Caliph, unless he has two entourage: an entourage that commands him to do good, and an entourage that commands him to do evil and encourages him to do it, so the infallible is the one who is infallible. By God Almighty” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7518","7563 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam informed us, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Ja’far, he said: Tell me Safwan, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “God has not sent a prophet, nor was he There will be no caliph after him, unless he has two entourages: an entourage that commands him to do good and forbids him from evil, and an entourage who does not deceive him. He was protected from the lining of evil, and he was protected.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7519","7564 Amr bin Uthman told us, he said: Baqiya told us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hussein, on the authority of al-Qasim bin Muhammad, he said: I heard my aunt, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever among you is assigned a job and God intends good for it, He will make him a minister.” He is righteous. If he forgets, he reminds him, and if he remembers, he helps him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7520","7565 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, saying: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Zubaid Al-Ayami, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ali, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent an army and appointed a man over them.” So he lit a fire and said: Enter it. Some people wanted to enter it, and the others said: We just fled from it. So they mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. Then he said to those who wanted to enter it: If you entered it, you would not cease to be there until the Day of Resurrection. And He said to the others: Good. Ibn Al-Muthanna said in his hadith: “Good words.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7521","7566 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Ja’far, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A Muslim must listen and obey, in what he likes and dislikes, unless he is commanded to disobey. If he is commanded With disobedience, there is neither hearing nor obedience.”"
"7522","7567 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Asim Al-Adawi, on the authority of Ka’b bin Ujrah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There will be princes after me, so whoever believes their lies and helps them For their injustice, it is not from me, and I am not from it, and it is not coming to my pond, and whoever does not believe their lies, and does not help them in their injustice, So he is from me and I am from him, and he returns to my basin.”"
"7523","7568 Harun bin Ishaq told us, he said: Muhammad told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Adawi, on the authority of Ka’b Ibn Ujrah said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to us when we were nine and four. One of the two was an Arab, and the other From the non-Arabs, and he said: Listen, have you heard that there will be princes after me, whoever enters upon them and confirms their lies, and helps them to He wronged them, so he is not of me and I am not of him, and he will not come to me at the Fountain, and whoever does not enter upon them, and does not believe in their lies, and does not help them in their Their injustice is from me and I from him, and the basin will return to me.” Muhammad told me, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Asim Al-Adawi, on the authority of Ka’b bin Ujrah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Muhammad told me, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Ibrahim Not by Al-Nakha’i, on the authority of Ka’b, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the like. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7524","7569 Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Alqamah, who is Ibn Murthid, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, “A man asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he had put his foot in stitches, which jihad is best? He said: A word of truth when spoken to.” \"unjust power\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7525","7570 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Ubadah ibn Al-Samit, He said: “We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a gathering, and he said: You pledge allegiance to me on the condition that you do not associate anything with God, nor steal, nor commit adultery. And he recited to them the verse, so whoever of you fulfills it, his reward is with God, and whoever does any of that wrong, God will cover it for him, then it is to God that He will punish him, if He wills. And if He wills, He will forgive him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7526","7571 Muhammad bin Adam bin Sulayman informed me, on the authority of Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Sa’id Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah On the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “You will be keen on the leadership, but it will be regret and sadness, so what a breastfeeding woman, “Wretched is Fatima.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7527","7572 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, he said: “I was walking with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Uqba, speak. So I said: What should I say, O Messenger of God? He remained silent about me, then He said: O Uqba, say. I said: What should I say, O Messenger of God? He remained silent, so I said: Oh God, return it to me. He said: O Uqba, say. I said. What should I say, O Messenger of God? He said: Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of Creation. So I recited it until I came to the end, then he said: Say, so I said: What should I say? O Messenger of God? He said: Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of Creation. So I recited it until I came to the end of it, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: That is: No one asks for anything like it, and no one seeks refuge with something like it."
"7528","7573 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Imran Aslam, on the authority of Uqba bin Aamir said: “I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was riding, and I placed my hands on his feet and said: Recite to me Surah Hud, or Surat Yusuf, and he said: You will not recite anything more conveyed by God Almighty than “Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of creation.”"
"7529","7574 Ahmad bin Saeed told us, he said: Wahb bin Jarir told us, he said: Ubayy told us, he said: I heard Yahya telling us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of my father. Imran Al-Tajibi, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, said: I said: O Messenger of God, recite to me from Surat Yusuf, or Surat Hud. He said: O Uqba. Read with: Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of Creation, for you will never recite a Surah more beloved to God Almighty and more eloquent to Him than it. If you are able not to If you miss it, do it.”"
"7530","7575 Mahmoud bin Khalid told us, he said: Al-Walid told us, he said: Abu Amr, who is Al-Awza’i, told us, on the authority of Yahya, who is Ibn Abu Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Al-Harith, said: Abu Abdullah told me that Ibn Abbas Al-Juhani told him that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said to him: “O Ibn Abbas, shall I not guide you, or he said: shall I not inform you of the best of what those seeking refuge with? He said: Yes, O Messenger of God, he said: “Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of creation,” and “Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind.” These are the two Surahs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7531","7576 Amr bin Uthman told us, he said: Baqiya told us, he said: Buhair told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Maadan, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, On the authority of Uqba bin Amir, he said: “I presented to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a grey-haired mule, so he mounted it and took Uqba to drive it with it. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Uqba: Read. He said: What should I read, O Messenger of God? He said: Read: Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of creation. } Of the evil of what He created {2}, so he repeated it to me, until I read it and he realized that I was not very happy with it, so he said: Perhaps you neglected it, so I did not do it. \"You pray like it.\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7532","7577 Mahmoud bin Khalid told me, he said: Al-Walid told us, he said: Ibn Jabir told me, on the authority of Al-Qasim Abi Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Uqba Ibn Amir, he said: “While I was leading the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a niqab turban, when he said: Won’t you ride, O Uqba? So I hurried. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to ride the vehicle of the Messenger of God, then he said: Will you not ride, O Uqba? I fear that it will be a sin. So he got off and I rode for a while, then I got off, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rode, and then he said: Shall I not teach you two of the best surahs? The people recited them to me, so he recited them to me: Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of creation, and Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind, and the prayer was established, so he came forward, recited them, then passed on. By me, he said: How did you see, O Aqab? Recite them every time you sleep and wake up."
"7533","7578 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told me, he said: Yahya told us, and he is the son of Adam, he said: Ibn Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Abdul Al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul-Rahman, who said: I heard Uqba bin Amir saying: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He recited salutations during prayer, and he said to me: Recite them whenever you sleep and whenever you get up. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7534","7579 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna informed us, saying: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed, saying: Yazid bin Roman told me, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir Al-Juhani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Aslami, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, placed his hand on his chest, then said : Say, he said: I did not know what to say, then he said to me: Say, I said: Say, He is Allah, the One, then he said to me: Say, I said: Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of creation {1 } From the evil of what He created {2} until I had finished, then he said to me: Say, he said: I said: Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind until I had finished, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Thus, seek refuge, for those who seek refuge have never sought refuge with anything like them. “Mukhtasar. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is a mistake. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7535","7580 Muhammad bin Ali told me, he said: Al-Qanabi told me, on the authority of Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sulayman, on the authority of Muadh bin Abdul Allah bin Khubayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, said: “While I was leading the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, his mount on an expedition, when... He said: O Uqba, speak, he said: So I listened, then he said: O Uqba, speak, so I listened, so he said it the third time, so I said: What should I say? He said:  Say, He is God, One. So he recited the surah until he concluded it, then he recited: Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of creation, and I recited with him until he concluded it, then he recited: Say. “I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind.” So I recited it with him until he concluded it, then he said: “No one seeks refuge in the like of them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7536","7581 Safwan bin Amr told me, he said: Ahmad bin Khalid told us, he said: Shayban told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, that he heard Muhammad Ibn Ibrahim, that Abu Abdullah informed him, that Ibn Amir al-Juhani informed him, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O son of Amer, shall I not tell you the best of what those who seek refuge with? I said: Yes, O Messenger of God. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Say.” I seek refuge in the Lord of creation, and say, I seek refuge in the Lord of people.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7537","7582 Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh informed us, saying: Ibn Wahb informed us, saying: Muawiyah bin Salih informed me, on the authority of Ibn Al-Harith means Al-Ala, on the authority of Al-Qasim, the client of Muawiyah, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, who said: “I was leading the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. His camel was on a journey, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Uqba, shall I not teach you the best of the two surahs ever recited? Teach me: Say I seek refuge in my Lord Al-Falaq, and Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind. He did not see me very pleased with them, so when he came down for the morning prayer, he led the morning prayer for the people with them, and when he finished The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned to me during prayer and said: O Uqba, how did you see?"
"7538","7583 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited them in the morning prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7539","7584 Amr bin Ali informed us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Muawiya told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Uqba bin Amer, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited in the morning prayer the following verse: Ham, the prostration.”"
"7540","7585 Musa bin Hazzam told us, he said: Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Jubayr, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, “He asked the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, about the two exorcists. Uqba said: So the Messenger of God believed us.” May God bless him and grant him peace, with them in the Fajr prayer.”"
"7541","7586 Ahmad bin Uthman bin Hakim told us, saying: Khaled bin Mukhlid told us, saying: Abdullah bin Suleiman Al-Aslami told me, on the authority of Muadh bin Abdullah bin Khubayb Al-Juhani, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir Al-Juhani, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “Oh Uqba, Say, I said: What do I say? He said: Say, He is Allah, One. Then he said: Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of creation, Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind, so he recited them. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then he said: The people do not seek refuge with someone like them, or the people do not seek refuge with someone like them."
"7542","7587 Hisham bin Yunus told us, he said: Al-Qasim bin Malik told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: “It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was seeking refuge from the eyes of man and the eyes of jinn, until the two exorcists descended. When they descended, he took them and left. “Nothing else.”"
"7543","7588 Amr bin Ali Abu Hafs told us, he said: Badal told us, he said: Shaddad bin Sa’id Abu Talha told us, he said: Sa’id told us Al-Jariri, he said: Abu Nadra told us, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “Read, O Jabir. I said: What should I recite? May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of God. He said: Recite: Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of creation, and Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind. So I recited them. He said: Read with them, and you will not read with anything like them."
"7544","7589 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Qais told us, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, On the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Verses have been revealed to me the like of which has never been seen: Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of creation, until the end of the surah, and Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of creation.” By the Lord of mankind, until the end of the surah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7545","7590 Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: I heard Al-Nu’man, on the authority of Ziyad Abi Asad, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The people did not seek refuge with the likes of these two surahs: Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of Creation, and Say, I seek refuge in “By the Lord of mankind.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7546","7591 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Shaddad bin Saeed told us, he said: Saeed al-Jariri told us, on the authority of Abu Nadra On the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “O Jabir, read with: Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of creation, and say, I seek refuge in Lord of the people, O Jabir, and you will never read anything like them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7547","7592 Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Hafs bin Maysarah told me, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, On the authority of Muadh bin Abdullah bin Khubayb, on the authority of his father, he said: “I was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the road to Mecca, and I was alone. From the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I approached him, and he said to me: Say, so I said: What should I say? He said: Say, I said: What should I say? He said: Say I seek refuge By the Lord of Al-Falaq, until he sealed it, then he said: Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind, until he sealed it, then he said to me: People do not seek refuge with anything better than the two of them.”"
"7548","7593 Ya’qub bin Ibrahim informed us, on the authority of Ibn Ulayya, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’ bin Al-Shakhir, “On the authority of a man, who said: He was in I was marching, but at noon there were few people, and people were following me. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, descended, and I descended, so he joined me after me and struck. My shoulders, and he said: Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of creation. So I said: Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of creation. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited it and I read it. With him, then he said: Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited it, and I read it with him, and he said: When I pray, recite With them, you will never read anything like them.”"
"7549","7594 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abu Asim told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, he said: Usayd bin Abi Usayd told me, On the authority of Muadh ibn Abdullah, on the authority of his father, he said: “A cold and darkness struck us, so we waited for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to lead us in prayer. Then he mentioned something that meant it, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out and said: Say, I said: What do I say? He said: Say, He is God, the One, when the evening comes. And when you become three, everything will be enough for you.”"
"7550","7595 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told me, he said: My father told us, he said: Haywa told me, he said: Abu Hani told me, that Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubli heard that he heard Abd Allah ibn Amr say: “The heart of the son of Adam is between two of the Most Merciful’s fingers. Like a single heart, which he can turn as he wishes. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O God, the Converter of hearts, direct our hearts to your obedience.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7551","7596 Imran bin Bakkar told me, he said: Abu Al-Mughirah told us, he said: Safwan bin Amr told us, on the authority of Shurayh bin Ubaid, that he heard Al-Zubayr Ibn Al-Walid narrated, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, who said: “Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fought or traveled, Then the night overtook him, and he said: O land of my Lord and your Lord is God, I seek refuge in God from your evil, from the evil of what is in you, from the evil of what He created in you, and from the evil of what is upon you. “I seek refuge in God from the evil of every lion, lion, serpent, and scorpion, and from the inhabitant of the land, and from the evil of a father and his children.”"
"7552","7597 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told me, he said: Al-Aswad bin Amir told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Ishaq, On the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O God, I seek refuge in You lest I die of grief, or Suffering, or drowning, or the devil tripping me upon death, or me dying from a sting,” said Abu Ja’far Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak: This is a mistake. He is Ibrahim bin Al-Fadl. Abu Abdul Rahman said: Ibrahim bin Al-Fadl is an abandoned hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7553","7598 Harun bin Abdullah and Musa bin Abdul Rahman informed us, saying: Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Al-Muthanna bin Saeed Al-Tai, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, he said: We said to Zaid bin Arqam: Tell us what you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: O God, I seek refuge in You from inability, laziness, cowardice, miserliness, senility, and torment. The grave, and the temptation of the Antichrist. Oh God, give my soul its piety. You are the best of those who purify it. You are its guardian and master. My Lord, I seek refuge in You from a heart that does not He is humbled, a soul that is not satisfied, knowledge that is not beneficial, a supplication that is not heard, or a supplication that is not answered.” Harun said: In his hadith: He replaced the pyramid, In love"
"7554","7599 Ubayd Allah bin Saeed and Ahmad bin Harb told us, saying: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, and Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Zayd bin Arqam, said: “I do not tell you except what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us. He said: O God, I seek refuge in You from: Inability, laziness, miserliness, cowardice, senility, and the torment of the grave. Oh God, give our souls its strength. You are the best of those who purify it. You are her guardian and her guardian. Oh God, I seek refuge in You. Ahmad said in his hadith: From knowledge that is not beneficial, and they all said: And from a soul that is not satisfied. And from a heart that is not humbled, and from a supplication that is not answered.”"
"7555","7600 Wasil bin Abdul-Ala informed us, on the authority of Ibn Fudayl, on the authority of Asim bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, he said: “It was when It was said to Zayd bin Arqam, “Tell us what you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I will not narrate to you anything except what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said.” He narrated it to us and commanded us to say it: O God, I seek refuge in You from: inability, laziness, miserliness, cowardice, and senility. And the torment of the grave. Oh God, give my soul its strength. You are the best of those who purify it. You are its guardian and master. Oh God, I seek refuge in You from: the soul. It is not satisfied, a heart is not humble, knowledge is not beneficial, and a call is not answered.”"
"7556","7601 Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh and Yunus told us, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, saying: Usama bin Zayd told me that Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir told him, he said: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Oh God, I ask you Useful knowledge, and I seek refuge in You from knowledge that is of no benefit.” The wording by Yunus (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7557","7602 Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Usama bin Zaid told me, that Suleiman bin Musa told him, on the authority of Makhoul, that he entered upon Anas bin Malik, and heard him mentioning that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praying and saying: “O God, help me.” What you have taught me, and teach me what will benefit me, and provide me with knowledge by which you will benefit me.”"
"7558","7603 Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh informed us, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, saying: Al-Layth narrated to me, that Sa’id Al-Maqbari narrated to him, on the authority of His brother, Abbad bin Abi Saeed, said that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was saying: “O God, I seek refuge in You.” Among the four: knowledge that is not beneficial, a heart that is not humble, a soul that is not satisfied, and a supplication that is not heard.”"
"7559","7604 Qutaibah bin Saeed told me, he said: Thana Khalaf is Ibn Khalifa, on the authority of Hafs, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He makes these supplications: “O God, I seek refuge in You from: knowledge that is not of benefit, a heart that is not humble, a supplication that is not heard, and a soul that is not satisfied.” He said: Then He says: Oh God, I seek refuge in You from these four. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7560","7605 Qutaibah bin Sa’id informed us, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of his brother Abbad bin Abi Sa’id, that he heard Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “O God, I seek refuge in You from the four: from knowledge that is of no benefit, and from a heart that is not He is humbled, and from a soul that is not satisfied, and from a supplication that is not heard.”"
"7561","7606 Muhammad ibn Adam informed us, on the authority of Abu Khalid, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “O God, I seek refuge in You from: knowledge that is not beneficial, from a heart that is not humble, from a soul that is not satisfied, and from a supplication that is not heard.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7562","7607 Ubayd Allah bin Fadalah bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: Yahya informed us, and he is the son of Yahya, he said: I am Al-Layth bin Saad, on the authority of Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of his brother Abbad bin Abi Saeed, that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: Oh God, I seek refuge in You from: knowledge that is not beneficial, from a heart that is not humble, from a soul that is not satisfied, and from a supplication that is not heard.”"
"7563","7608 Yazid bin Sinan told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, he said: Sufyan informed us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Abi Al-Hudhayl, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seek refuge from four things: from knowledge that is not beneficial, and from “A heart that is not humble, a supplication that is not heard, and a soul that is not satisfied.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7564","7609 Ubaid bin Wakee’ bin Al-Jarrah told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Sa’d bin Aws, on the authority of Bilal bin Yahya, on the authority of Shutair bin Shikal bin Humaid, on the authority of his father, said: I said: “O Messenger of God, teach me a supplication that I will benefit from.” He said: Say: O God, protect me from the evil of my hearing and my soul. “And my tongue, and my heart, and the worst of my semen,” meaning his remembrance."
"7565","7610 Al-Hasan bin Ishaq told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, he said: Saad bin Aws told us, he said: Bilal bin Yahya told me, that Shutair ibn Shakal told him, on the authority of his father, Shakl ibn Humayd, who said: “I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Prophet of God, teach me I seek refuge with Him, so he took my hand, then said: Say: I seek refuge in You from the evil of my hearing, the evil of my sight, the evil of my tongue, the evil of my heart, and the evil of my semen. He said: Until I preserved it. Saad said: And semen: its water. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7566","7612 Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Hilal told us, he said: Husayn bin Ayyash told us, he said: Zuhayr told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun said: The companions of Muhammad, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seek refuge from: cowardice.” And stinginess, and temptation of the heart, and the torment of the grave.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7567","7613 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ubayd Allah informed us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, on the authority of Omar, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seek refuge from: cowardice, stinginess, temptation of the chest, and the torment of the grave.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7568","7614 Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, he said: I heard Musab bin Saad, on the authority of his father, said: “He used to teach us five, and he used to say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray for them and say to them: O God, I seek refuge in You from stinginess, I seek refuge in You from cowardice, I seek refuge in You from being sent back to the most miserable life, and I seek refuge in You from the torment of \"the grave\""
"7569","7615 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Muadh bin Hisham, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, “The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, used to say: “O God, I seek refuge in You from: inability, laziness, miserliness, senility, the torment of the grave, and the temptation of \"life and death\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7570","7616 Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz informed us, saying: Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun. On the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seek refuge from five things: miserliness, cowardice, bad life, and temptation.” chest, and the torment of the grave.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7571","7617 Yahya bin Muhammad told us, he said: Hibban bin Hilal told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, On the authority of Amr bin Maymun Al-Awdi, he said: Saad used to teach his sons these words, just as a teacher teaches boys, and he says: “Indeed, the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he used to seek refuge in them after the prayer. O God, I seek refuge in You from stinginess, I seek refuge in You from cowardice, and I seek refuge in You That I be returned to the most miserable age, and I seek refuge in You from the temptation of this world, and I seek refuge in You from the torment of the grave.” So I told Musaab about it, and he believed him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7572","7618 Abu Hatim al-Sijistani told us, he said: Abdullah bin Raja told us, he said: Saeed bin Salamah told us, he said: Amr bin Abi Amr told me. Mawla al-Muttalib, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Muttalib, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, “Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called, he would say “O God, I seek refuge in You from worry, sadness, helplessness, laziness, miserliness, cowardice, exposing religion, and the oppression of men.”"
"7573","Ali bin Al-Mundhir told us, on the authority of Ibn Al-Fudayl, he said: Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Anas bin Malik said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had supplications that he would not abandon. He used to say: O God, I seek refuge in You from: worry and sadness. Inability and laziness, miserliness and cowardice, the predominance of debt, and the predominance of men.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7574","7620 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Jarir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Abi Amr, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had supplications that he would not abandon. He used to say: O God, I seek refuge in You from: worry, sadness, and helplessness.” And laziness, miserliness, cowardice, the predominance of debt, and the predominance of men.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7575","7621 Humayd ibn Masada informed us, saying: Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Humayd ibn Tarawayh, Anas said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He supplicates: O God, I seek refuge in You from: laziness, senility, cowardice, miserliness, the temptation of the Antichrist, and the torment of the grave. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7576","7622 Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala informed us, saying: Al-Mu’tamir told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He supplicates, saying: “O God, I seek refuge in You from: inability, laziness, senility, miserliness, and cowardice, and I seek refuge in You from the torment of the grave, and from the trials of life and death.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7577","7623 Muhammad bin Uthman told me, he said: Salama bin Saeed bin Atiya told me, he was the best of the people of his time, he said: Muammar bin told us Rashid Abu Urwa, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seek refuge most often.” From debt and sin. I said: O Messenger of God, how often do you seek refuge from debt? He said: He is someone who was in debt and told a lie. He made a promise but broke it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7578","7626 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Humaid told us, he said: Anas was asked, “About the torment of the grave, and about Al-Dajjal, he said: “The Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to say: O God, I seek refuge in You from: laziness, senility, cowardice, and stinginess. And the temptation of the Antichrist, and the torment of the grave.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7579","7627 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abu Asim told us, he said: Uthman al-Shaham told us, he said: Muslim bin Abi Bakra told me: “Oh God, I I seek refuge in You from: laziness and the torment of the grave. He said: O my son, from whom did you hear this? He said: I heard you saying them. He said: Time, for I am. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say to them: (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7580","7628 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, “The Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: O God, I seek refuge in You from: inability and laziness, miserliness and cowardice, old age, and the torment of the grave. And the temptation of life and death.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7581","7629 Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Al-Hader told us, he said: Asim Al-Ahwal told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam said: “I do not teach you except what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to teach us: O God, I seek refuge in You from: inability and laziness. And miserliness, cowardice, senility, and the torment of the grave. Oh God, grant my soul its piety. You are the best of those who purify it. You are its guardian and guardian. Oh God, I seek refuge in You from: a heart that is not humble, a soul that is not satisfied, knowledge that is not beneficial, and a supplication that is not answered.”"
"7582","7630 Abu Asim told us, he said: Hibban told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, On the authority of Sa`id bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: O God, I seek refuge in You from poverty. I seek refuge in You from poverty and humiliation, and I seek refuge in You from being unjust or being wronged.” Al-Awza’i disagreed with him."
"7583","7631 Mahmoud bin Khalid told me, he said: Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Abu Amr, he said: Ishaq bin Abdullah told me, he said: He told me Jafar bin Iyadh said: Abu Hurairah told me, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Seek refuge in God from poverty and lack. And humiliation, and to be unjust or to be wronged.”"
"7584","7632 Mahmoud bin Khalid told us, he said: Omar, who is Ibn Abdul-Wahid, told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, he said: Ja’far bin Iyadh told me, he said: Abu Hurairah told me, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Seek refuge in God from poverty, from poverty, from humiliation, and from being unjust or being wronged.”"
"7585","7633 Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, saying: Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith informed us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, on the authority of Ishaq, On the authority of Sa`id bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “O God, I seek refuge in You from poverty and poverty. And humiliation, and I seek refuge in You lest I be wronged or be wronged.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7586","7634 Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Musa bin Shaybah told me, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha said: Ja’far bin Iyadh told me that Abu Hurairah told him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said: “Seek refuge in God from: poverty, paucity, humiliation, and from being unjust or being wronged.”"
"7587","7635 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi told us, he said: Uthman told us, he said: Muslim told us, that he had heard His father, saying at the end of the prayer: “O God, I seek refuge in You from: disbelief, poverty, and the torment of the grave.” So I started praying to him with them, and he said: Oh My son, how did you hang up these words? I said: O father, I heard you calling for them at the end of prayer, so I took them from you. He said: So stick to them, O. My son, the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to invoke them at the end of prayer. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7588","7636 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Abu Usama told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would often supplicate with these words: O God, I seek refuge in You from the temptation of Hellfire.” And the torment of the Fire, and the trial of the grave, and the torment of the grave, and the evil of the trial of the Antichrist, and the evil of the trial of poverty, and the evil of the trial of wealth, Oh God, wash away my sins with water of ice and hail, and purify my heart from sins, just as you purified a white garment from filth, and keep a distance between me and My sins are as great as the distance between the East and the West. O God, I seek refuge in You from: laziness, senility, sin, and infatuation.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7589","7637 Muhammad bin Al-Ala informed us, he said: Ibn Idris informed us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: O God, I seek refuge in You from hunger, for it is miserable to be lost, and I seek refuge in You from betrayal. “It is a wretched lining.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7590","7638 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abdullah bin Idris told us, he said: Ibn Ajlan told us, and another mentioned on the authority of Sa’id bin Abu Sa`id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “O God, I seek refuge in You from hunger, for it is miserable.” The lost one, and from betrayal, for it is a wretched soul.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
